# .gm/prd.yml + .gm/mutables.yml: per-dispatch runtime state, rewritten on
# nearly every PLAN/EXECUTE/VERIFY dispatch -- same class as .gm/witness/
# and gm.db above (transient, regenerated, never durable source). Tracking
# it committed a near-full-file version on every single dispatch (970
# revisions, 743MB logical history for a currently-2.1MB file), roughly
# half of .git on-disk blob weight -- untracked here per this project own
# derived-stores-are-transient-never-tracked policy.
#
# The successors of those two files: PRD rows and mutables now live one file
# per row under .gm/prd/ and .gm/mutables/, so two lanes can never lose each
# other's row to one whole-file rewrite, and a resolved row's material moves
# into .gm/prd-log.jsonl / .gm/mutables-log.jsonl, append-only and hash-chained.
# The row folders are the same transient class as the files they replace. The chained
# logs (.gm/prd-log.jsonl, .gm/mutables-log.jsonl) are authored project state and are
# never ignored (MUST_STAY_TRACKED in rs-plugkit crates/plugkit-core/src/gitignore.rs).
.gm/prd.yml
.gm/mutables.yml
.gm/prd/
.gm/mutables/
.gm/prd.absorbed.json
.gm/mutables.absorbed.json
.gm/.gm-continue-count
# <<< plugkit managed
# embedding-generation markers and browser mutable state: derived, regenerated, never tracked
.gm/.embed-generation.*
.gm/browser-mutables.yml
.gm/pw-sock-*/

# agentplug-runner project-local runtime state (kv store, per-project
# plugin-dispatch spool) -- transient, regenerated every session, same
# category as .gm/pw-sock-*/ above
.agentplug/
.agentplug-kv/

# local dev-tool caches (codesearch index, opencode config+node_modules) --
# regenerable local state, same category as .agentplug/ above
.code-search/
.opencode/

# rs-learn/memorize derived binary store -- every live gm session dispatching
# mutable-resolve/prd-add/memorize perpetually grows this file; it is a
# rebuildable derived cache, not source, and had grown past GitHub's 50MB
# recommended limit while tracked (57.18MB, live-witnessed via a real
# git_push warning) -- untracked here, same rule as any other derived store
# per this project's own "derived stores are transient, never tracked" policy.
gm.db
gm.db-wal
gm.db-shm
gm.db-journal
# advisory lock owner record for gm.db (transient, rewritten per store writer)
.gm/gm.db.lock.owner

# in-process plugkit probe artifact (transient)
gm-plugkit/.gm/

# tessl tooling marker (foreign, not shipped)
skills/gm-skill/.tessl-plugin/

# browser verb profiles and state: per-run Chrome user-data dirs, large and never source
.gm/browser-*/
.gm/browser-profiles/
.gm/browser-profile-default/
.gm/browser-state/

# one-shot codesearch results and FSM rejection diagnostics written under .gm/
.gm/codesearch-result-*.json
.gm/fsm-graph-rejected.json

# stray gm runtime directories created inside skill folders
skills/.gm/
skills/gm/.gm/
# volatile per-project reorientation marker
.gm/dream-rsi/_any-session/
# Dream-RSI observations are runtime state: each dispatch appends to them, so tracking them rewrote tracked files on every dispatch. History keeps the earlier commits.
.gm/dream-rsi/
# audit sweep outputs (paper/verb rewrite proposals) are generated per run, not source
.gm/audit*/


# Chrome browser profile: extension asset paths exceed the Windows 260-char limit (git status os error 206)
.gm/browser-profiles/
# browser_cdp lease profile, created by agentplug-host browser_lease.rs at root/.gm/browser-cdp-profile
.gm/browser-cdp-profile/

# gm lean-walk runtime state (traversal progress and route caches, rebuilt each walk)
.gm/lean-walk/
.gm/lane-claims.json
.gm/lean-walk-v1-readonly/
.gm/lean-edge-walk.json
.gm/lean-edge-walk.progress
.gm/lean-traverse-route.json
.gm/disciplines/lean-walk/
.gm/disciplines/gm-ubiq-lean/

# memorize-fire generated recall memos (rebuilt from gm.db, which is untracked)
.gm/memories/mem-*.md

# config-source cache rotation: a rotated-out cache tree and its sync marker are left
# behind under a .stale name when the live tree is rebuilt
.gm/config-source-cache-default.stale-*/
*.sync.json.stale

# lean-walk traversal scratch: per-slice traverse/verdict/witness notes, rewritten each walk
.gm/traversal/

# subagent heartbeat directory: every subagent writes .gm/pool/<session>.live on start and
# deletes it on finish, so the directory holds no source (skills/gm/SKILL.md, pool protocol)
.gm/pool/

# editor settings folder: never tracked anywhere in this tree
.vscode/

# runtime witness log: appended by every session, never versioned
.gm/witness-log.md

# gm-prd receipts: per-row runtime audit trail, not versioned
.gm/receipts/

# runtime lane scratch and a nested repo that is not a project submodule
.gm/lane-build/
.gm/witness-out/
.wt-lanewait/
.wt-thrash/

# manual prd-log recovery copies: full duplicates of the live chained log, never source
.gm/prd-log.jsonl.*.bak

# subagent walk scratch left in the parent tree: find11/find1 walk workspaces, browser session
# leases, and fs/fsread probe outputs. Scratch only, never source.
.gm/find11-*/
.gm/find*-w*/
.gm/browser-cdp-sessions/
.gm/fs-append-*.txt
.gm/fsread-*.txt
.gm/find*-*/
find1-*/
# PRD and mutable logs are runtime state read from disk; never tracked
.gm/mutables-log.jsonl
.gm/expansion-audit.jsonl
.gm/agentplug-runner.log
.gm/hyg-candidate/

# repro scratch directories: runtime reproduction workspaces, never source
.gm/repro-1018/
.gm/instructions-parked-*/
